Andrew D. Hilton wrote:

>  At level 13, this means you have a 16/21 or
> about 76% chance of converting it.

Extremely interesting; thanks! I had no idea what the chances were. Up
to this point, I was under the mistaken impression that there was
*always* a significant chance of failing and therefore getting zapped
or something.

And so, in response to David Damerell's remark:

> It amazes me that you have not done this already. I
> always convert altars once I'm about XL 5.

... the sad, embarrassing fact is that after countless games, with only
two ascended barbarians to show for it, I have *never* converted an
altar (but see below). And so I've struggled through *many* games
without a co-aligned altar conveniently at hand. I always accommodated
myself to this reality of the RNG, rather than challenged it. Perhaps
this should qualify as a conduct of some sort! ;-)

Now, getting back to my originally posted problem. I took the advice of
so many, and found that a simple prayer got me out of this trouble, as
a cursed blindfold is considered to be a major trouble.

A short while later I converted my first altar. And yes, it was easy
:-) I proceeded to offer lots of monsters with a bunch of wands of
create monster, now that I had a neutral altar finally in the game.
Unfortunately, I created a spotted jelly, and absent-mindedly started
to hit it without really paying attention ("It's only a jelly! What can
go wrong?"). Of course, I wasn't watching my hitpoints, and I was dead
within about three whacks or something.

I was so thoroughly devastated, and disgusted with myself, that I
quickly fired up my last remaining barbarian save game from months ago,
and proceeded from the Wizard's Tower to Ascension. So now I've
ascended my third barbarian. I think I'm through with barbarians now,
and will focus for the time being exclusively on valkyries.

I find it interesting that someone can play the game for a long time,
and still be unaware of stuff like the ease of converting altars. Also,
on this last ascension, I came to find out that if Death hits you, you
lose max hitpoints. So entering Astral with loads of b!full healing is
very important for preparation, even if you never use any.

Again, thanks to everyone for their help. Rose the Valkyrie is gone,
but I still got YAAP!

